A||N||24||Seanh||NOS in my future? Oh yeah!||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||07-08-2001||01:41 AM||||First off, I know this topic has been beaten to death in the archives...please don't tell me to search..I do know how to..<P>After seeing the movie Fast and Furious, it has really made me reconsider my thoughts on putting NOS on my Fiero. If I did, it would be on a 2.8/3.1L, 110K, excellent compression and all around good running condition. Tranny is of course, my favorite, automatic. I was wondering, how long would my engine last with NOS? I'd say, 100-120hp shot, regular usage..I love to race any time the opportunity presents itself.<P>I know some say the engine can take it fine, others say it won't handle squat. So, from anyone who is running NOS on a stock or high milage engine, have you had any trouble?<P>What type of computer system would you reccomend? I saw they used laptops in the movie to contol thier systems. I have laptop, and would love to use it if I can find a system that will work with it. I don't want to blow all kinds of money on it though, just want something to keep me from blowing my engine or accidently spraying when I shouldn't. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||07-08-2001||02:18 AM||||If you stick with a 50-shot from what I hear you should be fine. Anything else is pushing it. But what do I know? I have never run NOS. I just observe what everyone else does.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Shaun41178||07-08-2001||02:33 AM||||I had an NOS dry kit on my Fiero for about 3 years and had no problems.  however I was only running a 70 shot and that was on a engine that had about 20k on it when I put it on and 50k on it when I took it off.<P>I think if you have a engine with 100k miles on it then you shouldn't go more then a 70 shot and would recommend staying with a 50.  No you don't need a laptop to control the nitrous.  What comes in the kit is good enough to give the desired effects and the laptops would be needed if you spent lots of time on a dyno to custom tune and had a custom computer to go back and forth between programs.  Like one for racing and one for normal driving.<P>I am sure Travis will give some input here too.<P>I have a NOS dry kit 5120 for sale for $300 plus shipping.  New it is like $500 plus.  Its complete with a bottle that has about 8 pounds of nitrous in it.  Bottle holds 10 pounds max.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR><A HREF="http://members.aol.com/Shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>Preferred Performance</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Seanh||07-08-2001||09:10 AM||||Did Trav put a wet kit on his engine with excellent results? I would almost be tempted to go that route, after hearing how happy he was with it. How much will those kits run me?<P>Shaun, that kit your selling, it has pretty much everything I need to do it, right? If not, what else will I need? What do you have to do to your timing to run NOS? I heard you have to change it, and then the car runs crappy for daily driving. That was my logic for having a computer system for it, so it could adjust my timing for racing. This kit is 70 shot right? I may be interested...||||reg||1
Z||000004||chester||07-08-2001||11:12 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Seanh:<BR><B>Did Trav put a wet kit on his engine with excellent results? I would almost be tempted to go that route, after hearing how happy he was with it. How much will those kits run me?<P>Shaun, that kit your selling, it has pretty much everything I need to do it, right? If not, what else will I need? What do you have to do to your timing to run NOS? I heard you have to change it, and then the car runs crappy for daily driving. That was my logic for having a computer system for it, so it could adjust my timing for racing. This kit is 70 shot right? I may be interested...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I've been looking at NOS systems for a while now and have decided on this setup.  Comes with its own programmable computer setup.  Adjustable nozzle from 25 to 180+ HP.<BR>You can check it out at <A HREF="http://www.venom-performance.com/VCN%202000.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.venom-performance.com/VCN%202000.htm</A> <P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">   <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension||||reg||1
Z||000005||Seanh||07-08-2001||11:31 AM||||Where are you buying that setup and how much will it set you back? That is just want I was looking for, but price is going to have to be my deciding factor...||||reg||1
Z||000006||chester||07-08-2001||11:37 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Seanh:<BR><B>Where are you buying that setup and how much will it set you back? That is just want I was looking for, but price is going to have to be my deciding factor...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Being that the setup is computer controlled, it is pricey.  Your looking at around $900-1000 for the setup. It does have some awsome features to it though!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Seanh||07-08-2001||11:43 AM||||Ooch...Actually, thats is a fairly descent price for a computerized setup, but I just don't have that kinda money to blow on it. I may get Shaun's system now, and perhaps save and upgrade to the VNC-2000 later if I feel a need. I would like to have higher then a 70 hp shot, but $300 for a 70 is a pretty good price I might just have to take. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Seanh||07-08-2001||01:35 PM||||Acutally, looking thru past threads, I found this to be a really informative one: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/006347.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/006347.html</A> <P>Now, thats got me convinced to buy a "wet" kit. I mean, the base price is only $449, and then the Asscessory pack is $260. I want that computer also, but would get only the above now, and buy the computer system for it when I get more money.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Shaun41178||07-08-2001||01:36 PM||||Yes the kit I am selling is complete.  It comes with jets for a 50,70,80 and 90 hp shots if you wanted as the kit is adjustable.  You have to retard the timing 2 degrees for every 50 hp of nitrous you use.  I just retarded my base timing to 8 degrees as the stock setting is 10 degrees when I ran my 70 shot and all worked well.  no the car does not run crappy with the timing retarded 2 degrees all the time.<P>If you wanted you could get a MSD boost timing master at least thats what I think it is called.  anyway you can tie it into your nitrous kit and when you activate the nitrous it can retard the timing however many degrees you want.  That way you can drive around with your timing normal or advanced a bit but when you use your nitrous the timing gets retarded.  You can get a MSD thing from summit or Jegs.<P>Yea Travis used a wet kit and it gave good results.  He had major exhaust mods and lots of dyno tuning to help him get big numbers.  But a wet kit will cost you around $450 or so.<P>Man I would stay away from the venom stuff.  I have heard a ton of bad things about their nitrous kit.  Plus at twice the cost of a regular nitrous kit its not worth it for this "computer".  Get a regular kit and install it properly and tune it on a dyno and you will have the same amount of power with less cost then the venom kit.  I am sure Travis can give more input about the venom stuff then I can.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Seanh||07-08-2001||01:47 PM||||I like the looks of Venom, but I wouldn't really pay that much for a little 'ol dry kit like that. <P>Shaun, that kit your selling, I'm still interested in if only as a tempory till I can afford a wet system complete, will it only fit a Fiero? I ask because I know someone who might be interested in it with a 3.1L 89 Grand Prix...So Brandon, what do ya say? Wanna have the fastest Prix in town. Would smoke Nic's new engine hands down.<p>[This message has been edited by Seanh (edited 07-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||Seanh||07-08-2001||02:53 PM||||If all the jets are included, I think I would jet it to 80 or 90. Wonder how long my engine will take that? <P>Also, I can't time my Fiero at all. After I built my engine, I had it timed at a shop because I can't see how you people can see the timeing marks from above, it doesn't look physically possible. Can anyone give me a guess as to how much I need to turn the distributor to achieve the desired timeing retard? ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Joe Torma||07-09-2001||11:32 PM||||In regards to aftermarket engine control...<BR>I have a Electromotive TEC-II system running my 3400(fwd) conversion.  It is an INCREDIBLE system.  Not too bad to wire, but not for the computer weary.  You control EVERYTHING.  From injector pulse to timing.  I think I am the only person with the modified 3.4 fwd pushrod engine to date.  If they took the computer from the donor car...they are severely limited by it.  <P>If you can retard your timing and feed MORE GAS in with the nitrous you should be ok.  you don't want to detonate.<P>With the TEC system you can(pretty sure) program it to control a optional solinoid for nitrous.  The system is not cheap.  The Tec is programmed by a laptop(or my integrated on-car computer system).  So it is like Fast and Furious(I am a manager of a movie theater--awesome movie), but not as dramatic.  What is dramatic is the fact that while the engine is running, you can change most of the settings and hit ENTER and hear the engine run totally different.<P>L8r<BR>Joe<BR>'86 SE 3400series 300hp<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 07-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||Seanh||07-10-2001||01:18 AM||||That sounds like somthing I'm intested in...Do they have a website about their products? How much is "not cheap"? I think I'm getting the MSD 6A box, but would like to look into this first.||||reg||1
Z||000014||1FST2M6||07-10-2001||09:01 AM||||STAY AWAY FROM VENOM! theya re smoke and mirrors and you'll just be tossing yout $ away. <A HREF="http://www.nitrouwarehouse.com" TARGET=_blank>www.nitrouwarehouse.com</A>  and talk to John. the wet kit i have is exponentially better than the dry kit i HAD... <P>i've worked with 4-5 Venom kits and 1 while the venom engineeres were working on the car.. not a single one work worth a crap. same with the rest of their products. (injectors/ and re-man ECUs excluded) kinda strange that Venom doens't even use their own stuff on their race car... it's all NOS was built at a Holley facility in Ca.  strange hunh. anywho... <P>I'm slap happy with my wet kit.. wasn't any more difficult to install than the dry.. the better your exhaust  the better you nitrous kit will work.. headers and 2.5" cat/muffler will do WONDERS! <P><BR>Tec-II are nice but not a nessesity unlesst your running lots of boost or lots of nitrous. Greg (friend with 3.8 S/C) has this on his car and came to the dyno with a WEAK 150hp and left ONLY with Ed tuning th ecomputer 215hp and gained over 70lbft. there are quiet a few race cars that come to the shop with either TEC systems or LINK or Motec. (oh for those that saw F&F Motec doens't make exhausts, and the green "turbo-nitrous" eclipse that they blew up was naturally aspirated.. sorry side tracked) <P>but if your dead set on nitrous management the Nitrous Express F.R.E.D. unit is the ONLY chatter box that will hold 100% when set to 100%.. the nos unit, jacobs master mind and the Venom will still chatter. a wet kit with a FRED will be faster than a nonregulated dual stage. I dont' work for NX they are in Texas i'm in Ga. i just can't belive how much better this is over my previous kit.  <BR> <BR>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fsthydrantsig.jpg">            <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A> <BR> <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 07-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||Joe Torma||07-10-2001||08:23 PM||||The MSD box works well.  I worked on someone's Turbo(out of a thunderbird)2.8Fiero and I think that is the one he had.  It has a retard dial control...very handy apparently.<P>I'll look into the NOS capabilities of the TEC II.  Costs over $1600.  It was my only choice, and I'm very happy with it!<P><BR>Joe||||reg||1
Z||000016||Alex4mula||07-10-2001||10:12 PM||||Can anyone tell me how many 1/4 mile runs will a bottle of NOS give me? How much it cost to refill? I'm getting more & more interested in this NX wet kit. Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>Alex4mula<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/p69fbfe3e99ec5a0b81c10afcc578ff95/fe6d5c42.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||Joe Torma||07-11-2001||03:06 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Alex4mula:<BR><B>Can anyone tell me how many 1/4 mile runs will a bottle of NOS give me? How much it cost to refill? I'm getting more & more interested in this NX wet kit. Thanks.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>How much NOS?  If you search for "quarter mile calculator" on any search engine, there are lots of estimators.  Enter the weight of your car and HP and viola...a kinda accurate figure.<P>NOS is nuts...an extra 100+ horses at the press of a button?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Joe<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000018||chester||07-11-2001||06:55 AM||||That is a good question, how much does it cost to refill lets say a 10 pound nitrous bottle?  How many 1/4 mile runs do you get to a bottle?||||reg||5
Z||000019||1FST2M6||07-11-2001||08:53 AM||||about 7 full 1/4 runs (at 50-70shot) and the rest will still be better than stock but not as good as the rest.. just MAKE sure your bottle stays around 80* for the best performance. here in atlanta i just refilled a bottle.. it was $29 ($2.70 a pound + tax) it last just about all weekend.. it'll SURELY pay for itself...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> thats what paid for most of the go fast my SE had... (dork in red 97 Lightning)"hey you wanna run that POS.." (me) "hehehe SUUUUURE.. if you think you stand a chance" if you push on a kids ego they'll pony up... <P><BR>oh uum.. street racing is bad don't street race...  mmm kay  ||||reg||1
